WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.670
He had been pacing back and forth all night,
so many hours spent walking to and fro in

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:09.190
his quarters that his feet were starting to
develop painful blisters.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:14.650
Yet Jace couldn’t bring himself to stay
still after his unsettling discovery.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.920
Over the course of the night, it had driven
him almost mad.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.449
But it wasn’t just the fear of the inevitable
calamity he had learned of that was keeping

00:00:22.449 --> 00:00:26.420
him up, and worrying him into a state of near
insanity.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:32.899
It was the lie, the smokescreen that had been
used to cover up the truth… and it came

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.149
all the way from the top.

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:40.149
Jace Jacobi had been working as a researcher
within the SCP Foundation for the better part

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:41.260
of a decade.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:46.880
Sure, it wasn’t an easy job at the best
of times; in fact, it could be dirty, dangerous,

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.520
and even downright deadly work.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:53.750
But Jace had learned to take comfort in the
bigger picture, and it cultivated in him a

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.300
loyalty for the Foundation and what they stood
for.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:02.180
The reassuring knowledge that he was playing
but one small part in protecting the world

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.990
from anomalous threats usually helped him
sleep a little easier at night.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.420
This was not one of those nights.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.229
Completely by accident, the researcher had
learned of a terrible truth.

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:18.150
He’d seen a lot of horrible things while
working at the Foundation, from one horrific,

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:22.590
endlessly regenerating omnicidal reptile
to a monstrous creature comprised primarily

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.950
of giant teeth protruding from its body.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:30.540
But what he had uncovered in the depths of
the SCP Foundation’s own archive, terrified

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.990
him for a whole different reason: because
it seemed to undo every good thing Jace and

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:39.950
all other personnel had done the name of the
Foundation.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:44.650
He believed that they were the good guys,
that their efforts were to prevent total global

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:45.719
destruction.

00:01:45.719 --> 00:01:49.969
Instead, it turned out they were just pawns.

00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:54.049
Being familiar with a whole filing cabinet’s
worth of special containment procedures for

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:58.409
various anomalies, Jace was familiar with
the term ‘220 Calabasas’.

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:02.840
He’d even almost been considered to receive
high enough security clearance to be given

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.299
the full details as to what it entailed.

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:09.950
He was aware already that was the name given
to a process that was required to be performed

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:16.420
by Foundation staff, as a way to keep SCP-2317
actively contained.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.850
SCP-2317 was a wooden door leading to another
dimension.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.790
Or at least, it appeared to be.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:28.700
After accessing some restricted files, a suppressed
secondary level of information hidden underneath

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:34.160
the SCP-2317 entry, Jace discovered what was
really going on.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:40.150
SCP-2317 was – in part – a Door to Another
World, as its nickname suggested.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.700
But that wasn’t the whole story.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:47.400
Beyond the door lay a barren salt plain, the
only structures visible for miles being seven

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:52.090
identical stone pillars with ancient symbols
carved into their surface.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:57.110
Frequently, a small group of Foundation personnel
and security staff would be sent into SCP-2317,

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:03.940
each one of them given a specific role to
undertake as they performed 220 Calabasas.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:08.260
That process required for active containment
was more like an occult ritual, involving

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:14.250
holy water, an obsidian-edged knife, chants
that invoked ancient powerful gods, and a

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.230
chicken to act as a live sacrifice.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:21.420
If Jace had just learned those specifics of
220 Calabasas, he wouldn’t have realized

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.390
that the ritual was actually a phony, even
a pretty convincing one at that.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:31.880
Buried beneath the pillars was chained something
of unspeakable, unknowable power.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:38.190
It had gone by many names, each invoking a
particularly nasty sense of trepidation.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:44.790
The Sire of Tyranny, Qiral Erîbav, or simply
the Devourer of Worlds.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.860
The 220 Calabasas ritual was supposedly a
way to keep the beast locked below, to strengthen

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:54.599
the seven chains each latching the ancient
monstrosity to the pillars above.

00:03:54.599 --> 00:03:59.650
Except it didn’t; it was a smokescreen,
the ritual did nothing to keep the shackles

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.739
of the Devourer intact.

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:07.080
There was but one chain remaining, one more
tether keeping the ancient beast caged.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:12.470
And over the years, no matter how many times
the Foundation performed 220 Calabasas, it

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.870
was eroding, getting weaker and weaker.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:20.370
It was inevitable: the Devourer of Worlds
would one day be free.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:24.540
And yet, that wasn’t even the worst part
about what Jace had uncovered.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:28.830
What could possibly be worse than learning
an eldritch deity intent on unfurling doom

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.979
couldn’t be contained with the one method
the Foundation had?

00:04:31.979 --> 00:04:37.669
Well, it was that the Foundation knew and
had known for a long time that 220 Calabasas

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:42.919
was nothing more than a charade, with all
the effectiveness of a band-aid over a broken

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:43.919
leg.

00:04:43.919 --> 00:04:48.039
As if that wasn’t bad enough, Jace had traced
the source of this cover-up right to the very

00:04:48.039 --> 00:04:54.509
top, to the highest operational level within
the SCP Foundation’s hierarchy; the O5 Council

00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:55.560
was responsible.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:01.260
They had known for a long, long time about
the ineffectiveness of 220 Calabasas, and

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:07.740
yet hadn’t pursued any more permanent solutions
to the looming threat posed by SCP-2317 and

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.990
the Devourer.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:12.419
After a sleepless night, Jace could hold it
in no longer.

00:05:12.419 --> 00:05:17.260
He had to tread carefully, given how far up
the chain this conspiracy went, it was hard

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.550
to know who to trust.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:24.070
Something had to be done, that much was clear
to him, whether that involved sealing or outright

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:27.220
destroying SCP-2317.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:31.440
But if those tasked with overseeing the entire
Foundation were in on this cover up, then

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:35.710
Jace had to be extremely careful about who
he went to for help.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:40.569
There was only one person he was certain he
could rely on, and share his findings with

00:05:40.569 --> 00:05:42.210
in secrecy.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:46.620
Senior Researcher Ellis had long been a good
friend of Jace’s; in fact, he’d even go

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:50.360
as far to say that Ellis was his only real
friend within the Foundation.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:55.050
The more experienced member of personnel had
practically mentored Jacobi from his earliest

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:57.370
days as an SCP researcher.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:01.900
Ellis had helped him get to grips with certain
difficult containment procedures, and even

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:06.410
taken the fall for Jace after some of his
early mistakes nearly caused a containment

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:07.550
breach.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:12.030
Researcher Ellis’ seniority meant he only
got away with a metaphorical slap on the wrist.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:17.509
But most crucially for Jace right now, Ellis
wasn’t a high enough rank to be even close

00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:23.030
to any of the upper echelon Foundation doctors
like Doctor Bright or Doctor Gears.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:26.650
Nor was he senior enough to have any direct
dealings with the O5 Council.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:30.810
If there was anyone working at the Foundation
that Jace could possibly confide in about

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:38.200
his findings regarding the truth behind SCP-2317
and 220 Calabasas, it was Ellis.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:42.940
And maybe, between them, the pair could put
their heads together and avert the catastrophe

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:45.520
of the Devourer’s inevitable escape.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.889
Jace was nervously pacing back and forth while
Ellis’ eyes were glued to the terminal in

00:06:49.889 --> 00:06:50.889
his quarters.

00:06:50.889 --> 00:06:57.940
He had shown him a saved copy of the full
archive entry on SCP-2317, detailing everything.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:02.600
Not just the steps required to perform 220
Calabasas, but the additional information

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:07.150
at the ritual didn’t work, and that the
O5 Council knew it.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:11.379
After a long, painful wait for Researcher
Ellis to scan through the entire file, he

00:07:11.379 --> 00:07:14.200
leaned back from the terminal screen and sighed.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.810
“Well, this is hardly ideal,” he stated
matter-of-factly.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.610
“Hardly ideal?”

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:24.069
Jace echoed, his fear of what this all meant
manifesting itself as a frustrated outburst.

00:07:24.069 --> 00:07:27.310
“I think you might be underestimating it
just a little there, Ellis!

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:31.030
This isn’t just some mild inconvenience
we’ve now got to live with, we’re talking

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:34.009
about the end of the world as we know it!

00:07:34.009 --> 00:07:35.009
XK-Class!

00:07:35.009 --> 00:07:40.430
And on top of that, the Council know it’s
coming and are doing nothing about it!

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:44.210
Instead, they’re making these high clearance
personnel go and pointlessly slaughter chickens

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:48.850
and recite meaningless prayers about ‘Seven
Seals, Seven Rings, Seven Thrones for The

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:49.850
Scarlet King’.”

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:52.310
“Jacobi, calm down,” Ellis replied sternly.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:54.379
“Let’s talk about this rationally.

00:07:54.379 --> 00:07:59.750
For all we know, this file here could be a
part of SCP-2317’s containment procedures.”

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:02.550
“That’s what I’m saying, the procedure
is ineffective!”

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:03.550
he argued.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.710
“Let me finish,” the senior researcher
responded calmly.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:11.430
“We know of dozens of other anomalies that
employ infohazardous or memetic effects.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:16.150
And sometimes, it’s not uncommon for entities
of such a nature, with capabilities to infect

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:23.060
information itself to be combated via the
use of deliberate, necessary misinformation.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:29.070
This file might not even be an accurate description
of SCP-2317, it could easily be a method for

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.810
containing something else.”

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.060
“No, that doesn’t…”

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:33.530
Jace paused, holding his forehead.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.350
“Sorry, all of this is giving me a headache.

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:37.090
Could I trouble you for some water?”

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:38.820
“Of course,” Ellis answered.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:42.339
He got up from his seat and filled a plastic
cup from a cooler in his quarters.

00:08:42.339 --> 00:08:46.519
While his back was turned, Jacobi didn’t
see Ellis slip something into the water.

00:08:46.519 --> 00:08:49.560
“Thanks, Ellis,” Jace said as he gulped
down the whole cupful.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:53.339
“Like I was saying, that theory of it being
a memetic threat doesn’t make sense.

00:08:53.339 --> 00:08:55.800
You’ve seen SCP-2317 from a distance.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:56.800
We both have.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:01.260
It’s a physical dimensional gateway; I mean,
‘A Door to Another World’ is literally

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:03.370
its codename, for god’s sake!

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:08.230
Why would there be a real door with an intangible
infohazard behind it?”

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.700
Ellis stroked his chin, pondering quietly.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:15.040
For a moment, Jace’s vision seemed to get
a little blurry, but he blinked it away.

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:21.851
“Okay, so if we take everything in the SCP-2317
file as gospel, then answer me this: what

00:09:21.851 --> 00:09:23.290
do you propose we do about it?”

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.290
his mentor asked.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:27.120
“We have to think, radically.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:31.240
Together I think you and I need to come up
with an alternate, permanent solution to the

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:32.600
impending threat posed by SCP-2317.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:38.399
Then, we present it to the O5 Council, storm
into their chamber if necessary, and demand

00:09:38.399 --> 00:09:39.910
them to implement it.

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:43.140
The next 220 Calabasas is scheduled for a
few hours from now.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:47.920
We need to bring them something that will
actually work, not just that performative

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.690
pantomime they put on as a smokescreen.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.490
Otherwise, Ellis…”

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:57.150
Jace paused a moment, hearing his own voice
crack with despair, “If we don’t, the

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.580
Devourer is going to destroy everything.”

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:04.829
“You said the words permanent solution,
elaborate for me, please,” Ellis responded.

00:10:04.829 --> 00:10:10.180
“Look, I think we have only two options,”
the frightened researcher said; Jace noticed

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:15.130
he was starting to feel drowsy, lightheaded
even, needing to shake himself to stay upright

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.130
and conscious.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:21.709
“We either find a way to seal SCP-2317,
or we destroy the Door to Another World outright.

00:10:21.709 --> 00:10:24.580
The 220 Calabasas procedure…

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:27.350
no, ritual?

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.740
Rit…-ual.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:35.149
They take a one kiloton nuke in with them
in case of containment failure, right?

00:10:35.149 --> 00:10:41.080
We detonate one of those inside that dimension,
pray that it kills the Devourer of Words…

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.080
Worlds.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:48.250
Then, we shut the door and blow that up behind
us too…”

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:52.600
Suddenly, Jace’s legs gave out underneath
him, like they couldn’t support his bodyweight

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:53.600
anymore.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.310
He landed on the floor with a thud, while
Ellis loomed over him with a sympathetic look

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:59.570
on his lined face.

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:02.510
“You… drug…

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:03.990
me?”

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.270
Jace barely managed to get the question out.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.529
“I’m sorry, Jacobi,” Ellis sighed.

00:11:08.529 --> 00:11:11.589
“Believe me when I say that I would have
preferred to talk you out of these seditious

00:11:11.589 --> 00:11:12.589
thoughts.

00:11:12.589 --> 00:11:14.750
But duty to the Foundation comes first.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:15.769
You understand.”

00:11:15.769 --> 00:11:19.180
The door opened, the heavy clomping of boots
against the floor.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:22.790
Jace could barely turn to see the squad of
security guards entering the room.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:27.709
They lifted his body up off the ground, getting
limper by the second, and began dragging him

00:11:27.709 --> 00:11:29.230
out by his arms.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:33.760
With all his waning strength, he kicked and
thrashed his legs as they trailed beneath

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:34.760
him.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:37.380
Being taken away by the guards, Jace yelled
for his mentor’s help.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:43.389
He kept trying until his voice became slurred,
imperceptible sounds, not even words anymore.

00:11:43.389 --> 00:11:48.420
The world around him started sinking into
darkness as whatever he’d been dosed with

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:49.970
took full effect.

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:55.180
As Jace was hauled off struggling, not once
did Ellis dare to look him in the eye.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:59.930
Jace had no idea how much time had passed,
only that he’d been chemically knocked unconscious

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:01.440
for most of it.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:06.360
Opening his heavy eyelids, he had no idea
where he was: the room around him was in pitch

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:07.360
darkness.

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:11.620
For a second, he wondered if he’d been executed
by the Foundation, and was currently dead,

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:14.699
his consciousness trapped in an endless, inky
void.

00:12:14.699 --> 00:12:19.160
Then another concerning thought pushed its
way into his head; had they thrown him into

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:20.649
the Devourer of Worlds’ prison?

00:12:20.649 --> 00:12:25.670
It was a cruel, callous move – even for
the SCP Foundation – to offer Jace up as

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:30.579
a sacrifice for daring to look further into
the truth behind SCP-2317.

00:12:30.579 --> 00:12:35.850
A column of light cut through the dark from
somewhere above him, gleaming down so bright

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:38.170
that it was hard to look directly at it.

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:42.020
The spotlight did little to illuminate the
rest of the room, although squinting through

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:46.839
the dark, the researcher could detect the
outlines of several figures sat in a circle,

00:12:46.839 --> 00:12:47.839
facing him.

00:12:47.839 --> 00:12:52.080
Thirteen of them, to be exact, with one extra
taking their seat.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:56.510
He was just awake enough to remember a crucial
detail that explained where he was: there

00:12:56.510 --> 00:13:01.660
were thirteen members of the O5 Council, along
with one Administrator.

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:06.380
“Hello again, Researcher Jacobi,” came
a voice from one of the seats encircling him.

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:09.730
“Tell us, do you know why you’re here?”

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:10.730
“Y-you…”

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:14.160
Jace stuttered, before his fear once again
erupted in an explosive outburst.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:17.790
“You all knew about SCP-2317!

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:22.510
You had us perform 220 Calabasas time and
time again, knowing that it was doing nothing

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:24.220
to keep the Devourer contained.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:26.070
If that creature gets loose…

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:30.050
no, when it does, it will destroy everything
and everyone.

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:33.620
The Foundation is meant to contain anomalies,
not pretend to!

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:38.570
We have a duty to every adult and child on
this planet to protect them from this entity.”

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:43.649
“Do not exposit the Foundation’s mandates
to us, Jacobi,” another of the councilmember’s

00:13:43.649 --> 00:13:47.949
voices replied, sounding not in the least
bit concerned – if anything, they sounded

00:13:47.949 --> 00:13:48.949
bored.

00:13:48.949 --> 00:13:53.490
“The SCP Foundation acts in accordance with
what this council dictates, not by whatever

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:56.779
moral framework you have chosen to impose
on this organization.”

00:13:56.779 --> 00:13:59.740
“But the Devourer of Worlds is coming!”

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:00.740
Jace pleaded.

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:02.350
“You all know as much!

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:07.980
I’ve seen it in the SCP-2317 file; inevitable,
you used that exact word.”

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:14.560
“We are aware of the threat faced by SCP-2317-K,
or the Devourer as you call it,” a third

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:15.740
councilmember interjected.

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:21.150
“But rest assured, at the time 220 Calabasas
was established to provide an illusion of

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:25.120
containment, we calculated it would take several
decades for the final chain holding the creature

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.180
to give way.”

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:28.650
“That time might have already elapsed!”

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:29.650
the researcher argued.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:33.860
“And in the meantime, we have no countermeasures
prepared, no strategy, and the rest of the

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:36.910
personnel have no idea that this threat is
coming.”

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:41.740
“Hmph, almost exactly the same wording as
last time,” one councilmember said, not

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:45.750
addressing the rest directly but still just
audible enough for Jace to detect it.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:49.640
“What do you mean ‘last time’?” he
asked, thinking back a few short moments to

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.060
the beginning of this exchange.

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:53.540
“Wait, why did you say ‘hello again’
when I woke up here?”

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:57.360
There was a horrible, nauseating silence through
out the room for a moment.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:01.940
Jace had already worked out the answer; why
would the Council bother telling him the truth

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:02.940
now?

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:05.910
“I’ve figured this out before, haven’t
I?” he said.

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:09.040
“A handful of times,” one of the voices
replied.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:12.410
“If not you, then another member of personnel.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:15.660
Every now and then someone snoops, uncovers
something they shouldn’t.”

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:19.300
“And you make them forget it,” Jace finished
their sentence for them.

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:22.820
“Before we apply the amnestics,” the voice
said.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:27.170
“Observe: today’s 220 Calabasas procedure
is already underway.”

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:31.990
A huge, curved screen blinked to life; it
filled half the circumference of the room,

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:36.750
but wasn’t enough to give Jace any clearer
of a look at the O5 Council.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:41.430
Each one of them was cast as shadowy, silhouetted
figures against the images now appearing on

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:42.430
the screen.

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:48.720
It was footage being streamed live from one
of the personnel cleared to enter SCP-2317.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:53.000
They were already in the middle of performing
the phony ritual, spritzing holy water over

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:57.330
the seven pillars; unaware that only one of
them was still linked to a chain keeping the

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:59.410
Devourer imprisoned below.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:03.790
Suddenly, there was a rumbling, a shaking
reverberating through the ground on the video

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:05.230
feed, like an earthquake...

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.750
or something moving underground.

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:09.930
“Oh my god,” Jace breathed as he watched
in horror.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:10.930
“It’s happening!

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:11.970
The Devourer is coming now!

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:13.360
Get them out of there!”

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.480
Some of the O5s mumbled awkwardly to themselves.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:19.820
“We shouldn’t act with too much haste,
it could just be the creature reacting to

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:21.760
the ritual,” one hypothesized.

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:26.160
“It’s been imprisoned for longer than
a lot of us have lived, it’s bound to get

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:27.389
restless,” another concurred.

00:16:27.389 --> 00:16:31.190
“Besides, the security team are armed with
a nuclear device in case the worst should

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.190
happen.”

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.380
On the screen, the tremors were continuing.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:38.519
The personnel member in charge of applying
the holy water dropped the silver aspergillum

00:16:38.519 --> 00:16:43.339
and aspersorium containing it, spilling its
content over the salted earth below.

00:16:43.339 --> 00:16:47.959
Without any further warning, the ground started
to crumble in the feed, an enormous clawed

00:16:47.959 --> 00:16:50.240
hand bursting up from underground.

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:55.589
It was followed by the hulking shape of something
much larger breaking through the salt plain,

00:16:55.589 --> 00:17:00.120
sending a tidal wave towards the personnel
member whose bodycam footage was being displayed.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:03.220
The feed cut out, and the room was dark once
again.

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:07.940
“It’s too late,” Jace stared at the
council in a mix of terror and disgust.

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:10.929
“You did nothing, and now it’s too late!”

00:17:10.929 --> 00:17:16.010
Before any of them could reply, another tremor
rang out, this time beneath Jace’s own feet.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.870
The Devourer of Worlds was here.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:23.429
It was bursting through the wooden door of
SCP-2317, and tearing the Foundation facility

00:17:23.429 --> 00:17:26.169
apart with its immense size as it emerged.

00:17:26.169 --> 00:17:31.429
The walls cracked, the entire building beginning
to crumble around him and the O5 Council,

00:17:31.429 --> 00:17:35.870
who were all hurriedly exiting the chamber
to whatever plans or bunkers they had to ensure

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.830
their own personal survival.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:43.260
Suddenly, the huge weight of something dropped
through the dark and collapsed on top of Jace.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:47.919
Standing up among the wreckage of the obliterated
building, the Devourer of Worlds drew itself

00:17:47.919 --> 00:17:49.539
up to its full height.

00:17:49.539 --> 00:17:53.990
It was an impossibly-large creature, humanoid
and obese.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:58.669
Its entire body was covered head-to-toe in
thick, armored scales, with horns atop its

00:17:58.669 --> 00:18:00.110
jawless head.

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:05.370
From one of them hung the final chain, a withered
shackle no longer keeping the monster held

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:07.420
within its underground prison.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.490
The seven chains had all failed.

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:16.100
The ritual, 220 Calabasas, had failed; in
fact, it never worked in the first place.

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:21.150
Far below, his arms pinned painfully under
a heavy slab of concrete, Jace stared up at

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.640
the towering form of the Devourer.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:28.419
He had felt scared as the building came down
around him, and even now, there was a lingering

00:18:28.419 --> 00:18:29.910
fear of his own death.

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:34.720
But there was something else there too, a
sense of feeling oddly relieved.

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:39.169
Not necessarily glad to be right about the
impending doom, or even pleased to know this

00:18:39.169 --> 00:18:42.290
ancient, trapped deity was about to destroy
the whole planet.

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:46.549
But at least the Devourer of Worlds was honest,
he thought.

00:18:46.549 --> 00:18:52.790
There was no subterfuge, no rituals acting
as a smokescreen, no more lies.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:59.280
Just an honest, simplicity of a creature whose
only goal was to bring an end to everything.

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:04.730
As Jace watched, the Devourer raised its hands
up, reaching the highest pinnacle of the sky,

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:07.330
then brought them straight back down to Earth.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:12.919
It plunged both deep into the skin of the
world, deep enough to crack the very surface

00:19:12.919 --> 00:19:18.360
open, mantle and magma were spewing everywhere
like blood from the gaping wounds it left

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:19.420
in the planet.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:24.420
Jace Jacobi closed his eyes, as the ground
beneath where he lay trapped ripped open,

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:26.880
he plummeted into the dark.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:33.890
Now go and check out “SCP-2317 THE DEVOURER
OF WORLDS/A DOOR TO ANOTHER WORLD” and “SCP-2440

00:19:33.890 --> 00:19:35.780
THE SEALED KING” for more eldritch horrors
that will destroy your mind!

